{
  "name": "happy",
  "integration": "maze-security",
  "description": "One page of investigations exercising both id spaces the grouping code can produce: the asset_id segment of scanner_finding_hash, and the asset_name of a related scanner finding. Proves two investigations sharing one scanner_finding_hash asset collapse onto a single asset carrying both vulnerabilities, that a single investigation fans out to one asset per related finding, that OS name and version are lifted out of vulnerability_root_cause_analysis, and that finding metadata (asset_type, cloud_platform, region, account_id, scanner) is carried onto the asset.\n\nThe fourth investigation carries an empty scanner_finding_hash and no related findings, so it names no asset. It used to become an asset keyed on its own investigation id -- one asset per finding, since an investigation is one CVE against one thing -- and is now skipped and logged.\n\nnamespaced_ids is skipped: Maze ids are bare scanner-supplied names with no tenant scope. Under no-id-match they no longer drive matching, so the collision hazard the invariant guards is not reachable through this integration.",
